WSTCSTPAPR.NS 0.0978 Small and below   rank 2019-02-28  589 Smallcap 100  BUY yes
Step 3. The three signals at 2019-03-08 (latest Master row of each index on or before it): Nifty 100 SELL (row dated 2019-03-08), Midcap 100 BUY (row dated 2019-03-08), Smallcap 100 BUY (row dated 2019-03-08) -> pattern SBB.
Step 4. n = 10 stocks held (Large 1, Mid 1, Small and below 8); k = 9 of them sit in a band whose index is BUY. FS = k / n = 9 / 10 = 0.900.
        The rule decides in integers: IN iff 5k >= 3n: 5 x 9 = 45 against 3 x 10 = 30 -> IN. (FS weighted by listed weights, 0.902, is R6 only.)
        The three-index switch looks at the pattern only: SBB is not BBB -> OUT. So this is an 'extra' week: the rule is IN while the switch is OUT.
Step 5. The trade: decided at the close of 2019-03-08, made on the next session, 2019-03-11 (session no. 47 of 1932), at each instrument's OHLC4 = (open + high + low + close) / 4 of that session. The book held OUT (50% GOLDBEES, 50% cash).
        V = the book's value at that session's fill prices before cost = 1.007796 (NAV starts at 1.000 on 2019-01-02). Target for stock i = V x w_i (GOLDBEES and cash 0). Sold: the whole sleeve, 1.007796; bought: 1.007796 of stocks; traded = sum of |target - current| = 2.015591.
        cost = traded x 20.8 / 2 / 10,000 = 2.015591 x 0.001040 = 0.002096; every new position is scaled by (V - cost) / V = 0.99792000; units_i = V x w_i x 0.997920 / OHLC4_i.
